/// Iterator combinators.
///
/// This package grows the iteration vocabulary on top of the core `Iterator`
/// and `Iterable` traits (which live in `std/builtin`). Every combinator is
/// lazy and single-pass unless noted, returns a concrete iterator that is
/// itself `Iterable`, and composes with the others.
///
///     from "std/itertools" import enumerate, zip, filter, take
///
///     for (i, x) in enumerate([10, 20, 30]) { print(i, x) }
///     for (a, b) in zip([1, 2, 3], "ab") { print(a, b) }
///     for x in filter([1, 2, 3, 4], is_even) { print(x) }
///     for x in take([1, 2, 3, 4], 2) { print(x) }
///
/// `reduce` is the exception: it consumes its source eagerly and returns a
/// single folded value rather than an iterator.